    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0409" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v04/pg383"/>

                <head>184. Telegram From the Embassy in Vietnam to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d184-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-10-06T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                                1963, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>642. 1. Your 534.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d184-f2"/></p>
                <p>2. An excellent instruction outlining a course of action which should yield
                    constructive results.</p>
                <p>3. I plan to let the continued suspension of the Commodity Import Program become
                    evident without my calling attention to it in so many words. I am credibly
                    informed that it is worrying Diem now, and that he will have to speak to me
                    about it.</p>
                <p>4. In general, U.S. representatives in Saigon will handle specific matters in
                    accordance with your para. 10.</p>
                <p>5. I am calling key Country Team members together tomorrow and am passing your
                    cable to them individually now.</p>
                <p>6. Assume this supersedes previous telegram concerning suspension or cutting off
                    of aid.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d184-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
